  clock: 3  # 18cd
  nonce: 18cd  # 18cd
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (mechanism confirmed; the family is far larger than 8-11 nodes).\nDispatch relocated: analyze/base.py:1724 populate_kind_stable_ids; map _KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES at base.py:1701 (file/module/dependency/variable/export/project/interface/type + class/struct/enum/trait/protocol/contract + template). base.py:1749-1751 `if factory is None: continue` -- no default arm, and the docstring (:1737-1744) states it as policy: \"New kinds that surface with None need their own factory entry here.\" No commit since filing touches the map (git log -S_KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES --since=2026-08-01: none).\nSelf-survey of this repo at 134a06d505: none_cohort 11 (same 11 as the 09-25 entry: json/package 3 incl. packages/htrac-frontend/package.json, proto/message 2, toml/package 2, proto/method 1, csharp/property 1, erlang/function 1, bash/alias 1); validation_report.stable_id_stats collision_rate_pct 0.0, none_cohort_pct 0.02.\nNEW, and bigger: the erlang/function null is not one node -- it is EVERY function of whole languages. Tiny fixture survey (2-3 functions per file): clojure 2/2, elixir 2/2, erlang 3/3, haskell 2/2, ocaml 2/2, zig 2/2 functions have stable_id None (none_cohort_pct 56.52 on that fixture); their module/file nodes are stamped. The self map hides this because those languages appear there only as one-file fixtures. erlang.py never sets stable_id (no \"stable_id\" string in the file); 27 analyzer modules that emit function kinds contain no \"stable_id\" (grep -L, heuristic, not each verified) incl. commonlisp, fsharp, elm, qml, thrift, gdscript, lean, agda, circom, wolfram, llvm_ir.\nSo \"function\" (and \"method\", \"property\", ...) are absent from the backstop map AND these producers never call compute_stable_id. A default arm fixes the null; it does not by itself give those languages the typed (ADR-0035) formula their siblings get.\nProposed update: retitle around \"whole-language function populations ship stable_id None (clojure/elixir/erlang/haskell/ocaml/zig at least)\"; the 8 -> 11 count is a self-repo artefact. Related: WI-banod (config-family analyzers stamp composite ids), INV-dulah."  # 18cd
